## DESCRIPTION
## Implicit function theorem
## ENDDESCRIPTION

## DBsubject('Calculus - multivariable')
## DBchapter('Differentiation of multivariable functions')
## DBsection('Implicit function theorem')

DOCUMENT();

loadMacros("PGstandard.pl", "PGML.pl", "parserPopUp.pl");

TEXT(beginproblem());

$mc_yes = PopUp(["?", "Yes", "No", "Inconclusive"], "Yes");
$mc_inc = PopUp(["?", "Yes", "No", "Inconclusive"], "Inconclusive");

BEGIN_PGML


Let [` F(x,y,z) = x^3+3xyz+z^2y-4y-5z+4 `]. Note [` F(1,1,1) = 0 `] and [` \nabla F(1,1,1) = (6,0,0) `].

1. Does the equation [` F(x,y,z) = 0 `] locally define [` z `] as a [` C^1 `] function of [` (x,y) `] near the point [` (1,1,1) `]? [_]{$mc_inc}

2. Does the equation [` F(x,y,z) = 0 `] locally define [` y `] as a [` C^1 `] function of [` (x,z) `] near the point [` (1,1,1) `]? [_]{$mc_inc}

3. Does the equation [` F(x,y,z) = 0 `] locally define [` x `] as a [` C^1 `] function of [` (y,z) `] near the point [` (1,1,1) `]? [_]{$mc_yes}
END_PGML

$showPartialCorrectAnswers = 0;

BEGIN_SOLUTION
For the first two, the implicit function theorem does not apply and we cannot know definitively without further (difficult) exploration.
END_SOLUTION

ENDDOCUMENT();